{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgdZDDHy27xygQDy79Ers","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Apple has just entered smart home and home security with a new product line built in collaboration with LG and Schneider Electric, and Amazon has updated its smart home lineup with new AI-powered home cameras. Into that market comes Thrive Holdings, which has agreed to buy ADT for $10 per share, about $7.6 billion in equity and $15.3 billion in enterprise value according to ADT.\n\nADT's position is unusual for a company about to change owners. It already partners with Apple and Google and is expected to keep those relationships, so two of the large technology companies shaping the category are also ADT's partners. Thrive Holdings, which describes its mission as holding companies long-term and revitalizing them with AI, now owns the business that sits between those partners and its customers. The article does not say how the new owner plans to handle that, and it names no products. The only stated direction is that ADT will form the foundation of Thrive Holdings' smart home security business.\n\nOpenAI's role is the other piece. It is both an investor in Thrive Holdings and a partner that supplies models, technology and forward-deployed engineers to the companies Thrive owns. Whether that support reaches ADT in a specific form is an inference, since the announcement says only that new products are planned. Even so, the structure points to how ADT's AI work could be staffed.\n\nThe article treats AI-powered physical security as a category in motion, with offerings ranging from Apple's and Amazon's home products to startups selling AI dog robots as roving security guards. ADT's new owner has so far announced an intention to invest and release products, in a market where established competitors have already shipped theirs."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":971,"cache_read_input_tokens":2838,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":971},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ac73c352-fd96-4d7c-bc31-f780d655bd73","uuid":"797b1a1e-115d-4f05-9f95-3d719f6dbffe","timestamp":"2026-11-02T05:33:47.535Z","request_id":"req_011CgdZDD5p59vGqFri4amc3"}
